### Space Race JE widgets — the milestone panels, mounted on nine journal entries.
###
### Every milestone entry attaches three named roots from this file, in the UN's
### shape (un_layout_widget.gui):
###   custom_widget_container_1  widget_je_space_race_<m>_overview   the overview
###   custom_widget_container_2  widget_je_space_race_<m>            the live sections
###   custom_widget_container_3  widget_je_space_race_reference      How the Space Race Works
### The overview sits above the entry's one-line status text, the live sections
### below it. The waiting entry (je_space_race_interstellar_results) has no
### controls and no live sections: an overview and the reference only. The
### reference root is one widget shared by all nine entries.
###
### Each section is a type (te_sr_sec_*); te_sr_status_sections and
### te_sr_reference_sections set their order, and te_sr_overview_milestone /
### te_sr_overview_transit compose the overview. What differs between
### milestones is only data (which scripted GUI the controls address, which
### script values and loc keys the panel reads), passed as sr_* blockoverrides
### by one pair of types per milestone (te_sr_<m>_overview, te_sr_<m>_status).
### The roots at the foot of this file wrap those, and the Timeline Extended
### window's Space Race tab (gui/te_systems_window.gui) instances the same
### types, so the two hosts draw one body. Vanilla ships several named widgets
### in one journal-entry widget file
### (gui/journal_entry_widgets/ep2_japan_widgets.gui:501,550 mounted by
### 00_meiji_restoration.txt:10,16).
###
### The panels replace the vanilla button grid, which is hidden from humans:
### every space race scripted button carries `is_ai = yes` in its `visible`, so
### the AI still picks its approach and funding through the buttons' ai_chance
### while a player sees only this. That makes the mapping an obligation — all
### four of the buttons' actions per milestone have a control here
### (te_sr_sec_control), and a fifth the grid never had:
###
###   op 0  Safe approach        op 2  funding −
###   op 1  Ambitious approach   op 3  funding +
###   op 4  Standard approach (player only; every milestone starts on it)
###
### The table is repeated in common/scripted_guis/space_race_sguis.txt; keep the
### two in step. Neither side holds a rule: every op delegates to the shared
### sr_possible_* trigger and sr_effect_* effect that the journal-entry buttons
### call, so the grid and the panel cannot drift.
###
### DATA CONTRACT — everything shown comes from script, nothing is re-derived:
###   state (status cell) -> ScriptValue('sr_disp_status_<m>'), read from
###                          sr_<m>_last_status, whose single derivation site
###                          is sr_set_milestone_status_base; its tooltip is the
###                          matching sr_pace_note_* sentence, and Safe and
###                          Ambitious carry their weekly cost in the word
###                          (sr_disp_cost_*_<m>)
###   progress / goal     -> ScriptValue('sr_progress_<m>_value'), ('sr_<m>_goal');
###                          the bar reads sr_disp_progress_frac_<m>, the same
###                          two numbers as a 0..1 fraction
###   pace                -> ScriptValue('sr_pace_rate_<m>'), the rate the pulse
###                          actually applies
###   setback risk        -> ScriptValue('sr_risk_shown_<m>'), the value the roll
###                          uses, forced to zero during the post-setback review
###   the first           -> ScriptValue('sr_disp_first_claimed_<m>')
###   setbacks, estimate  -> sr_setbacks_<m>_value, sr_eta_months_<m>
###   mission profile     -> GetCustom('sr_<m>_profile')
###   reward preview      -> GetStaticModifier('sr_first_<m>').GetDesc in the
###                          progress bar's tooltip, never a typed number
###   who else is racing  -> five estimate rows: the order and each rival's
###                          capital from sr_rivals_estimate_refresh (the viewer's
###                          sr_rival_total_<m>, sr_rival_<m>_<1..5>), the numbers
###                          from sr_disp_rival_{est,lo,hi}_<m> with the rival
###                          passed in (AddScope 'sr_rival'); beyond five, the
###                          sr_rivals_sgui list on hover, because `.gui` has no
###                          verified way to list countries (gotchas #11, #15)
###   programme row       -> ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_<m>'); each icon's
###                          tooltip is GetCustom('sr_prog_<m>'). The
###                          interstellar icon's four states read
###                          sr_disp_prog_interstellar
### The sr_disp_* values are in common/script_values/space_race_display_values.txt.
###
### COST. The Rivals rows read stored slots and evaluate three small script
### values each per frame; the full list (sr_rivals_sgui, which walks every
### country) renders only on the "+N more" hover. The monthly refresh that
### fills the slots runs for players only.
###
### Widths are fixed, never content-sized: every root and composer is 520
### wide (`minimumsize`), each panel's content 480, and rows of numbers use
### fixed columns, so nothing shifts when a value changes length.
###
### Every root is gated on `[JournalEntry.IsActive]`: all nine entries carry
### `is_shown_when_inactive`, so a widget is otherwise built for countries that
### hold none of the space race's variables — the failure mode that produced
### ~1,000 "Failed to fetch variable" errors on the UN chamber's first in-game
### test (docs/guides/gui_modding_guide.md gotcha #14).
###
### Collapse flags say their default (test_space_race_layout.py): *_closed
### sections are open until closed, *_open ones collapsed until opened. The live
### sections' flags are per milestone (`sr_panel_control_<m>_closed`,
### `sr_panel_rivals_<m>_closed`), because several milestone entries can be
### active at once; the shared reference has one (`sr_panel_how_open`). They
### live in GetVariableSystem, which is client-side, never saved and invisible
### to script.

types space_race_widget_types
{
	### ======================================================================
	### PRIMITIVES (shapes copied from un_chamber_widget.gui)
	### ======================================================================
	type te_sr_text = textbox {
		autoresize = yes
		multiline = yes
		minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
		maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
		align = left|nobaseline
		using = fontsize_medium
	}

	type te_sr_panel = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		parentanchor = hcenter
		spacing = 2
		margin = { 20 8 }

		background = {
			using = entry_bg_fancy_dark
			alpha = 0.5
		}
	}

	type te_sr_section_header = section_header_button {
		blockoverride "layout" {
			parentanchor = hcenter
			size = { 520 38 }
		}
	}

	### A heading inside a section's panel, with a faint rule under it
	### (un_chamber_subheader).
	type te_sr_subheader = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 1
		block "subheader_margin" {
			margin_top = 10
		}

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			multiline = yes
			maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_large
			default_format = "#title"
			block "subheader_text" {}
		}
		divider_clean = {
			blockoverride "size" {
				size = { 480 2 }
			}
		}
	}

	### Explanatory text under a heading (un_chamber_note). Static keys only.
	type te_sr_note = textbox {
		autoresize = yes
		multiline = yes
		minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
		maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
		align = left|nobaseline
		using = fontsize_medium
		default_format = "#lore"
	}

	### A table row: a label on the left and its value on the right
	### (un_chamber_value_row), the value column wide enough for the longest
	### figure, an estimate of "1300 months".
	type te_sr_value_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		margin = { 4 1 }

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 330 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 330 -1 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			elide = right
			block "row_label" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 130 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 130 -1 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			default_format = "#v"
			block "row_value" {}
		}
	}

	### One approach option. `action_binding` carries the four properties that
	### address the scripted GUI, because they are the only part that differs
	### between the three options; the sizing is shared (110 + 3 × 116 + 3 × 4
	### fits the 480 content width).
	type te_sr_action_button = button {
		using = default_button_action
		size = { 116 30 }
		parentanchor = vcenter

		textbox = {
			parentanchor = center
			align = center|nobaseline
			autoresize = yes
			max_width = 106
			elide = right
			using = fontsize_small
			block "action_label" {}
		}

		block "action_binding" {}
	}

	### ======================================================================
	### OVERVIEW PIECES
	### ======================================================================

	### A cell of the overview's first row: an icon, its word small beneath
	### (te_un_ov_icon_label). Fixed width, so the row cannot push the panel
	### wider: three cells fill the 480 column (3 × 156 + 2 × 6), so the longest
	### word ("Ambitious −360/wk") fits without "..." (round 3;
	### test_space_race_labels.py holds every label to its cell). `icon_alpha`
	### dims the icon.
	type te_sr_ov_icon_label = widget {
		size = { 156 58 }

		icon = {
			size = { 36 36 }
			parentanchor = top|hcenter
			block "icon_alpha" {}
			block "icon_texture" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			parentanchor = bottom|hcenter
			autoresize = yes
			max_width = 154
			elide = right
			align = hcenter|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_small
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			block "label" {}
		}
	}

	### "The first": open (lit) or claimed by another power (dimmed). The
	### instance sets which one shows; the tooltips are the sentences the
	### Rivals list used to open with.
	type te_sr_ov_first = flowcontainer {
		ignoreinvisible = yes

		te_sr_ov_icon_label = {
			block "first_open" {}
			tooltip = "sr_rivals_first_open"
			blockoverride "icon_texture" {
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/first.dds"
			}
			blockoverride "label" {
				text = "je_space_race_widget_ov_first_open"
			}
		}
		te_sr_ov_icon_label = {
			block "first_claimed" {}
			tooltip = "sr_rivals_first_claimed"
			blockoverride "icon_alpha" {
				alpha = 0.25
			}
			blockoverride "icon_texture" {
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/first.dds"
			}
			blockoverride "label" {
				text = "je_space_race_widget_ov_first_claimed"
			}
		}
	}

	### Progress towards the goal: a label, the bar and the headline
	### ("124 / 200 (+3.5/mo)"); the tooltip is on the whole row, as the UN's
	### authority row. The bar ends at the goal, so it needs no target marker.
	### Fixed columns (110 + 140 + 210, with the spacing 476), so a longer number
	### never moves the bar. The label column fits the longest label, "Next
	### Colony"; the headline column the longest figure, "650 / 650 (+99.9/mo)"
	### (round 3: "Next Colony" was cut to "Next Colo..." at 90). The tooltip's
	### block is "row_tooltip", not "bar_tooltip": that name is the history
	### charts', whose bar tooltips have no JournalEntry to read
	### (test_history_chart_tooltip_context.py).
	type te_sr_ov_bar_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		spacing = 8
		parentanchor = hcenter
		block "row_tooltip" {}

		textbox = {
			minimumsize = { 110 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 110 -1 }
			autoresize = yes
			elide = right
			parentanchor = vcenter
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			block "bar_label" {}
		}
		default_progressbar_horizontal = {
			size = { 140 18 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			blockoverride "values" {
				block "bar_value" {}
				min = 0
				max = 1
			}
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 210 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 210 -1 }
			elide = right
			parentanchor = vcenter
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			block "bar_text" {}
		}
	}

	### A share of the 34 worlds as a framed pie (te_un_ov_pie, with a third
	### layer): the disc is the unclaimed rest, then every world claimed, then
	### ours on top — largest first (gui_modding_guide.md, "Pie charts of
	### script-held data"). The textures: docs/systems/space_race_gui_icons.md.
	type te_sr_ov_pie = widget {
		size = { 150 108 }

		icon = {
			size = { 86 86 }
			parentanchor = top|hcenter
			texture = "gfx/interface/backgrounds/round_frame_dec.dds"
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 62 62 }
			parentanchor = top|hcenter
			position = { 0 12 }

			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				value = 1
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/pie_unclaimed.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				block "pie_claimed" {}
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/pie_claimed.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				block "pie_ours" {}
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/pie_ours.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
		}
		textbox = {
			parentanchor = bottom|hcenter
			autoresize = yes
			align = hcenter|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			block "pie_label" {}
		}
	}

	### One entry of the programme row: its journal icon (PR #571) at full
	### colour once achieved, half while under way, faint otherwise, with a
	### flag in the corner when we were first. The instance sets the texture
	### on the three icons and the code tests that pick one.
	type te_sr_ov_prog_cell = widget {
		size = { 50 50 }

		icon = {
			size = { 44 44 }
			parentanchor = center
			block "lit" {}
			block "prog_texture" {}
		}
		icon = {
			size = { 44 44 }
			parentanchor = center
			alpha = 0.6
			block "running" {}
			block "prog_texture" {}
		}
		icon = {
			size = { 44 44 }
			parentanchor = center
			alpha = 0.25
			block "unlit" {}
			block "prog_texture" {}
		}
		icon = {
			size = { 18 18 }
			parentanchor = top|right
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/first_mark.dds"
			block "first" {
				visible = no
			}
		}
	}

	### The Interstellar Probe and the wait for its data, one cell with four
	### states (owner's play-test, round 3). Each state is its own icon, with
	### its own texture and hover, shown by one equality test on
	### sr_disp_prog_interstellar, so no two can show at once: 0 not begun,
	### 1 under way, 2 launched and awaiting data, 3 data received. Each
	### state's art (PR #586, space_race_gui_icons.md) carries the state, so
	### none is faded. The flag marks a first, as in te_sr_ov_prog_cell, and
	### lets the hover through to the state beneath it.
	type te_sr_ov_prog_cell_interstellar = widget {
		size = { 50 50 }

		### 0: not begun, or another power finished it first
		icon = {
			size = { 44 44 }
			parentanchor = center
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/interstellar_not_begun.dds"
			tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_prog_interstellar_0"
			visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_interstellar'), '(CFixedPoint)0' )]"
		}

		### 1: under way
		icon = {
			size = { 44 44 }
			parentanchor = center
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/interstellar_under_way.dds"
			tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_prog_interstellar_1"
			visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_interstellar'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
		}

		### 2: launched, awaiting data
		icon = {
			size = { 44 44 }
			parentanchor = center
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/interstellar_awaiting_data.dds"
			tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_prog_interstellar_2"
			visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_interstellar'), '(CFixedPoint)2' )]"
		}

		### 3: data received
		icon = {
			size = { 44 44 }
			parentanchor = center
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/interstellar_data_received.dds"
			tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_prog_interstellar_3"
			visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_interstellar'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
		}

		icon = {
			size = { 18 18 }
			parentanchor = top|right
			alwaystransparent = yes
			texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/first_mark.dds"
			visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_interstellar_probe'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
		}
	}

	### The whole programme, eight icons in a row under a centred label: the
	### same on every panel. Each icon's tooltip is the row of the old
	### "programme so far" list (name and state, sr_prog_<m>). The Interstellar
	### Probe and its wait for data share the seventh icon, which has four
	### states of its own (te_sr_ov_prog_cell_interstellar). Code order:
	### space_race_display_values.txt, sr_disp_prog_*.
	type te_sr_ov_programme = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		spacing = 2
		parentanchor = hcenter
		minimumsize = { 480 -1 }

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			parentanchor = hcenter
			align = hcenter|nobaseline
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			text = "je_space_race_widget_programme_header"
			tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_ov_programme_tt"
		}
		flowcontainer = {
			direction = horizontal
			spacing = 3
			parentanchor = hcenter

			te_sr_ov_prog_cell = {
				tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_prog_suborbital"
				blockoverride "prog_texture" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/event_icons/je_space_race_suborbital.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "lit" {
					visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_suborbital'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "running" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_suborbital'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "unlit" {
					visible = "[And( Not( GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_suborbital'), '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ), NotEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_suborbital'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ) )]"
				}
				blockoverride "first" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_suborbital'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
				}
			}
			te_sr_ov_prog_cell = {
				tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_prog_orbital"
				blockoverride "prog_texture" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/event_icons/je_space_race_orbital.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "lit" {
					visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_orbital'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "running" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_orbital'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "unlit" {
					visible = "[And( Not( GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_orbital'), '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ), NotEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_orbital'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ) )]"
				}
				blockoverride "first" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_orbital'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
				}
			}
			te_sr_ov_prog_cell = {
				tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_prog_moon_landing"
				blockoverride "prog_texture" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/event_icons/je_space_race_moon_landing.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "lit" {
					visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "running" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "unlit" {
					visible = "[And( Not( GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ), NotEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ) )]"
				}
				blockoverride "first" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
				}
			}
			te_sr_ov_prog_cell = {
				tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_prog_probe"
				blockoverride "prog_texture" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/event_icons/je_space_race_probe.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "lit" {
					visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_probe'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "running" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_probe'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "unlit" {
					visible = "[And( Not( GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_probe'), '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ), NotEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_probe'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ) )]"
				}
				blockoverride "first" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_probe'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
				}
			}
			te_sr_ov_prog_cell = {
				tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_prog_moon_base"
				blockoverride "prog_texture" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/event_icons/je_space_race_moon_base.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "lit" {
					visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_base'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "running" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_base'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "unlit" {
					visible = "[And( Not( GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_base'), '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ), NotEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_base'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ) )]"
				}
				blockoverride "first" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_moon_base'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
				}
			}
			te_sr_ov_prog_cell = {
				tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_prog_mars_landing"
				blockoverride "prog_texture" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/event_icons/je_space_race_mars_landing.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "lit" {
					visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_mars_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "running" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_mars_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "unlit" {
					visible = "[And( Not( GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_mars_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ), NotEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_mars_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ) )]"
				}
				blockoverride "first" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_mars_landing'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
				}
			}
			te_sr_ov_prog_cell_interstellar = {}
			te_sr_ov_prog_cell = {
				tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_prog_solar_colonization"
				blockoverride "prog_texture" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/event_icons/je_space_race_solar_colonization.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "lit" {
					visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_solar_colonization'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "running" {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_solar_colonization'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "unlit" {
					visible = "[And( Not( GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_solar_colonization'), '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ), NotEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_prog_solar_colonization'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ) )]"
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### ======================================================================
	### OVERVIEW COMPOSERS
	### ======================================================================

	### The overview of a milestone with controls (eight entries). Row 1: the
	### state, the setback risk, and "the first" (or, for colonization, the
	### stage); row 2: progress; then any extra rows (colonization's worlds
	### pie); then the programme. The datacontext is the milestone's scripted
	### GUI, set on the root. While it is not shown (solar colonization held
	### open for its colony modifiers, or its production method switched off),
	### the state reads Idle and the risk and progress rows are hidden.
	type te_sr_overview_milestone = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		minimumsize = { 520 -1 }
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"

		te_sr_panel = {
			spacing = 10

			### Row 1
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = horizontal
				spacing = 6
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				parentanchor = hcenter

				### The state: one cell of five shows.
				te_sr_ov_icon_label = {
					visible = "[Not( ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End ) )]"
					tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_ov_idle_tt"
					blockoverride "icon_texture" {
						texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/state_idle.dds"
					}
					blockoverride "label" {
						text = "je_space_race_widget_ov_idle"
					}
				}
				flowcontainer = {
					ignoreinvisible = yes
					visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"

					te_sr_ov_icon_label = {
						block "sr_status_standard" {}
						tooltip = "sr_pace_note_standard"
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/state_standard.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							text = "je_space_race_widget_standard_label"
						}
					}
					### Safe and Ambitious carry their weekly cost in the word
					### (round 2: "make that clear").
					te_sr_ov_icon_label = {
						block "sr_status_safe" {}
						tooltip = "sr_pace_note_safe"
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/state_safe.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							block "sr_label_safe" {}
						}
					}
					te_sr_ov_icon_label = {
						block "sr_status_ambitious" {}
						tooltip = "sr_pace_note_ambitious"
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/state_ambitious.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							block "sr_label_ambitious" {}
						}
					}
					te_sr_ov_icon_label = {
						block "sr_status_shielded" {}
						tooltip = "sr_pace_note_shielded"
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/state_shielded.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							text = "je_space_race_widget_ov_shielded"
						}
					}
				}

				### Setback risk: lit while the monthly roll is made, faint at 0%.
				flowcontainer = {
					ignoreinvisible = yes
					visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_ov_risk_tt"

					te_sr_ov_icon_label = {
						block "sr_risk_lit" {}
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/risk.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							block "sr_risk_label" {}
						}
					}
					te_sr_ov_icon_label = {
						block "sr_risk_unlit" {}
						blockoverride "icon_alpha" {
							alpha = 0.25
						}
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/space_race_icons/risk.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							block "sr_risk_label" {}
						}
					}
				}

				### The first (seven milestones) or the stage (colonization).
				block "sr_third_cells" {}
			}

			### Row 2: progress, while the programme runs.
			te_sr_ov_bar_row = {
				visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
				blockoverride "row_tooltip" {
					block "sr_progress_tooltip" {}
				}
				blockoverride "bar_label" {
					block "sr_progress_label" {}
				}
				blockoverride "bar_value" {
					block "sr_progress_value" {}
				}
				blockoverride "bar_text" {
					block "sr_progress_text" {}
				}
			}

			block "sr_extra_rows" {}

			te_sr_ov_programme = {}
		}
	}

	### The waiting entry's overview: the transit and the programme.
	type te_sr_overview_transit = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		minimumsize = { 520 -1 }
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"

		te_sr_panel = {
			spacing = 10

			te_sr_ov_bar_row = {
				blockoverride "row_tooltip" {
					tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_ov_transit_tt"
				}
				blockoverride "bar_label" {
					text = "je_space_race_widget_ov_transit_label"
				}
				blockoverride "bar_value" {
					value = "[FixedPointToFloat( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('sr_disp_progress_frac_interstellar_results') )]"
				}
				blockoverride "bar_text" {
					text = "je_space_race_widget_progress_interstellar_results"
				}
			}

			te_sr_ov_programme = {}
		}
	}

	### ======================================================================
	### LIVE SECTIONS (open by default)
	### ======================================================================

	### Mission Control: the approach selector and the funding stepper, the
	### figures they move, and the mission profile.
	###
	### The controls, the setbacks and the estimate are gated on the scripted
	### GUI's is_shown, which is the same gate the milestone's four
	### journal-entry buttons use. That is what keeps the funding cell's `Var`
	### read safe, and what hides them when solar colonization drops into
	### passive mode with every colony claimed or its method off; the estimate
	### would otherwise quote a pace nothing is adding.
	type te_sr_sec_control = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		parentanchor = hcenter
		spacing = 2

		te_sr_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "je_space_race_widget_control_header"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				block "control_onclick" {}
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				block "control_showmore" {}
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				block "control_showless" {}
			}
		}

		te_sr_panel = {
			block "control_visible" {}

			flowcontainer = {
				direction = vertical
				spacing = 4
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
				visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"

				### Approach — ops 4 (Standard), 0 (Safe) and 1 (Ambitious),
				### beside their label. The option already in force greys itself
				### out through is_valid, and its tooltip says so (IsValidTooltip,
				### then what it does and what it costs a week). The two rows are
				### left-aligned so their labels form one column.
				flowcontainer = {
					direction = horizontal
					spacing = 4
					ignoreinvisible = yes

					textbox = {
						text = "je_space_race_widget_approach_label"
						size = { 110 30 }
						align = left|nobaseline
						using = fontsize_medium
						parentanchor = vcenter
						elide = right
					}

					te_sr_action_button = {
						blockoverride "action_label" {
							text = "je_space_race_widget_standard_label"
						}
						blockoverride "action_binding" {
							visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ).End )]"
							enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ).End )]"
							onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ).End )]"
							tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ).End ) ) )]"
						}
					}

					te_sr_action_button = {
						blockoverride "action_label" {
							text = "je_space_race_widget_safe_label"
						}
						blockoverride "action_binding" {
							visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
							enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
							onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
							tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End ) ) )]"
						}
					}

					te_sr_action_button = {
						blockoverride "action_label" {
							text = "je_space_race_widget_ambitious_label"
						}
						blockoverride "action_binding" {
							visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
							enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
							onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
							tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End ) ) )]"
						}
					}
				}

				### Funding — op 2 down, op 3 up, beside their label. The ceiling
				### is sr_max_funding_level, read by the shared trigger the minus
				### and plus buttons both ask.
				flowcontainer = {
					direction = horizontal
					spacing = 4
					ignoreinvisible = yes

					textbox = {
						text = "je_space_race_widget_funding_label"
						size = { 110 26 }
						align = left|nobaseline
						using = fontsize_medium
						parentanchor = vcenter
						elide = right
					}

					button_icon_minus_action = {
						size = { 26 26 }
						parentanchor = vcenter
						visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End )]"
						enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End )]"
						onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End )]"
						tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End ) ) )]"
					}

					textbox = {
						block "funding_value" {}
						size = { 84 26 }
						align = center|nobaseline
						using = fontsize_medium
						parentanchor = vcenter
						elide = right
					}

					button_icon_plus_action = {
						size = { 26 26 }
						parentanchor = vcenter
						visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End )]"
						enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End )]"
						onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End )]"
						tooltip = "[Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End ) ) )]"
					}
				}
			}

			### The figures pace and risk leave out (both are in the overview).
			te_sr_value_row = {
				visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
				blockoverride "row_label" {
					text = "je_space_race_widget_setbacks_label"
				}
				blockoverride "row_value" {
					block "setbacks_value" {}
				}
			}
			te_sr_value_row = {
				visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
				tooltip = "je_space_race_widget_eta_tt"
				blockoverride "row_label" {
					text = "je_space_race_widget_eta_label"
				}
				blockoverride "row_value" {
					block "eta_value" {}
				}
			}

			### The mission profile. Its heading keeps its top margin only
			### when the controls are above it, so the section never opens on
			### an empty line.
			te_sr_subheader = {
				visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "je_space_race_widget_profile_header"
				}
			}
			te_sr_subheader = {
				visible = "[Not( ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End ) )]"
				blockoverride "subheader_margin" {}
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "je_space_race_widget_profile_header"
				}
			}
			te_sr_text = {
				block "profile_text" {}
			}
		}
	}

	### One rival in the Rivals section: its name, its estimated progress as a
	### band with a marker, and the band in words; the tooltip says it is an
	### estimate and what narrows it. The name has the whole 480 line to
	### itself, because a country's name can run to 48 characters ("United
	### Socialist Council Republics of California"), which no column beside a
	### bar holds without "..." (round 3; test_space_race_labels.py). The bar
	### and the band in words share the line beneath, in fixed columns
	### (380 + 92, with the spacing 480), so nothing shifts as the numbers move.
	###
	### The bar is two layers and a marker: a white bar to the top of the band,
	### the plain bar to its bottom over it (its own background and frame
	### blanked, as the UN tally's upper layers do), and the marker at the
	### estimate (the marker technique of the UN's authority bar). The row's
	### `visible` is on the outer widget and the rival's capital, the
	### datacontext, on the inner one, so a slot that is not filled is never
	### read (the UN's Security Council seats do the same).
	type te_sr_rival_row = widget {
		size = { 480 42 }
		block "row_visible" {}

		flowcontainer = {
			direction = vertical
			spacing = 2
			block "row_context" {}
			block "row_tooltip" {}

			textbox = {
				minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
				maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
				autoresize = yes
				elide = right
				align = left|nobaseline
				using = fontsize_medium
				default_format = "#tooltippable"
				text = "je_space_race_widget_rival_name"
			}
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = horizontal
				spacing = 8
				widget = {
					size = { 380 14 }
					parentanchor = vcenter

					white_progressbar_horizontal = {
						size = { 100% 100% }
						blockoverride "values" {
							block "row_hi" {}
							min = 0
							max = 1
						}
					}
					default_progressbar_horizontal = {
						size = { 100% 100% }
						blockoverride "background" {}
						blockoverride "frame" {}
						blockoverride "values" {
							block "row_lo" {}
							min = 0
							max = 1
						}
						blockoverride "on_top_of_the_progressbar" {
							progressbar = {
								noprogresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
								progresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
								size = { 100% 100% }
								skip_initial_animation = yes
								direction = horizontal
								block "row_est" {}
								min = 0
								max = 1
								marker = {
									icon = {
										size = { 24 18 }
										parentanchor = vcenter
										widgetanchor = center
										texture = "gfx/interface/progressbar/progressbar_marker.dds"
									}
								}
							}
						}
					}
				}
				textbox = {
					minimumsize = { 92 -1 }
					maximumsize = { 92 -1 }
					autoresize = yes
					elide = right
					parentanchor = vcenter
					align = right|nobaseline
					using = fontsize_medium
					block "row_range" {}
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### Rivals: every other power whose programme is running this milestone
	### and moving, the first five as estimate rows (te_sr_rival_row; the order
	### and names from sr_rivals_estimate_refresh, space_race_effects.txt),
	### then "+N more", whose tooltip is the whole list (sr_rivals_sgui, only
	### walked on hover). Whether "the first" is still open is the overview's.
	type te_sr_sec_rivals = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		parentanchor = hcenter
		spacing = 2

		te_sr_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "je_space_race_widget_rivals_header"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				block "rivals_onclick" {}
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				block "rivals_showmore" {}
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				block "rivals_showless" {}
			}
		}

		te_sr_panel = {
			block "rivals_visible" {}

			te_sr_text = {
				block "rivals_none" {}
				text = "sr_rivals_none"
			}
			te_sr_rival_row = {
				blockoverride "row_visible" {
					block "rival_1" {}
				}
				blockoverride "row_context" {
					block "rival_1_context" {}
				}
				blockoverride "row_tooltip" {
					block "rival_tooltip" {}
				}
				blockoverride "row_lo" {
					block "rival_lo" {}
				}
				blockoverride "row_hi" {
					block "rival_hi" {}
				}
				blockoverride "row_est" {
					block "rival_est" {}
				}
				blockoverride "row_range" {
					block "rival_range" {}
				}
			}
			te_sr_rival_row = {
				blockoverride "row_visible" {
					block "rival_2" {}
				}
				blockoverride "row_context" {
					block "rival_2_context" {}
				}
				blockoverride "row_tooltip" {
					block "rival_tooltip" {}
				}
				blockoverride "row_lo" {
					block "rival_lo" {}
				}
				blockoverride "row_hi" {
					block "rival_hi" {}
				}
				blockoverride "row_est" {
					block "rival_est" {}
				}
				blockoverride "row_range" {
					block "rival_range" {}
				}
			}
			te_sr_rival_row = {
				blockoverride "row_visible" {
					block "rival_3" {}
				}
				blockoverride "row_context" {
					block "rival_3_context" {}
				}
				blockoverride "row_tooltip" {
					block "rival_tooltip" {}
				}
				blockoverride "row_lo" {
					block "rival_lo" {}
				}
				blockoverride "row_hi" {
					block "rival_hi" {}
				}
				blockoverride "row_est" {
					block "rival_est" {}
				}
				blockoverride "row_range" {
					block "rival_range" {}
				}
			}
			te_sr_rival_row = {
				blockoverride "row_visible" {
					block "rival_4" {}
				}
				blockoverride "row_context" {
					block "rival_4_context" {}
